#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192592 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b99d07-5914-578b-9aaf-f028ada5bee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14220" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation\n$-3 \\mid 1-x \\mid -2 = -8$.\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$\\mid 1-x|=k$\n\nWhat is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side:\n\nFirst, we add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 - x & -2 &= -8 \\\\ -3 & 1 - x & -2 + 2|=-8 + 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 - x & |=-6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3 \\mid 1 - x \\mid &= -6 \\\\\n\\frac{-3 \\mid 1 - x\\begin{vmatrix}}{-3} &= \\frac{-6}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{-3 \\mid 1 - x\\end{vmatrix}}{-3}|= 2 \\\\\n\\mid 1 - x \\mid &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution"}] :question/id #uuid "89382e45-4e78-554f-88e1-2bbf281617e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-14223" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\n1. $\\mid 1-x \\mid = -5$\n2. $\\mid 1-x \\mid + 5 = 2$\n3. $\\mid 1-x \\mid = 3$" :question/worked-solution "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left-hand side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n- Equation II *has no solution*. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n$\\mid 1 - x \\mid + 5|= 2; \\mid 1 - x \\mid |=-3$\nSince the right-hand side is *negative*, this equation has *no* solution.\n- Equation III has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "de2efe4f-e236-5fb2-bc46-eb037ecf26b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14228" :question/problem "Solve the equation $2 \\mid 2a - 4 \\mid - 7 = 13$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\begin{vmatrix}2a - 4 & -7 &= 13 \\\\ 2 & 2a - 4\\end{vmatrix}|= 20 \\\\\n\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $\\mid 2a-4 \\mid = 2a-4$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid |= 10; 2a - 4|= 10; 2a|= 14; a|= 7$\n- If $\\mid 2a-4 \\mid = -(2a-4)$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid |= 10; - (2a - 4)|= 10; - 2a + 4|= 10; - 2a|= 6; a|=-3$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=-3$ and $a=7$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" :knowledge-point/title "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ee0c8bd5-1086-5d70-85b2-9d89fb5fe3c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191269}] :question/id #uuid "e5a53e17-d1d0-5fa9-8d04-0b459a7ec9bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-212480" :question/problem "Consider the absolute value equation\n$2 - \\mid x + 2|= 7$.\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$\\mid x + 2|=$\n{{field-1}}"}]}
